  "scope": "For every measurable event of positive standard Gaussian probability p in any finite dimension, the Frobenius norm of its actual normalized centered second-moment tensor is at most 4*exp(1)*(1+log(1/p)). Both product and Euclidean Gaussian formulations are derived. The proof uses actual hypercontractivity, exact indicator norms, concrete Hermite coefficient decay and the proved degree-two tensor identity. No convexity, boundary regularity, dimension bound, spectral assumption or moment-transfer premise is supplied."
